%S A402839 0,0,0,0,0,4,4,4,4,4,4,6,6,6,8,8,8,10,10,10,12,12,12,14,14,14,14,15,
%T A402839 15,16,16,16,18,18,19,20,20,20,20,20,20,20,20,22,22,22,22,24,24,24,24,
%U A402839 27,27,29,30,31,31,31,31,32,32,32,32,32,33,34,34,38,38,39,39
%N A402839 Maximum number of terms in a sum of signed unit fractions with distinct denominators in {1, ..., n} that equals 0 and has no nonempty proper subsum equal to 0.
%C A402839 The empty sum is allowed, so a(n) = 0 when no nonempty sum satisfies the conditions.
%H A402839 Thomas F. Bloom, <a href="https://www.erdosproblems.com/319">Erdős Problem 319</a>, Erdős Problems.
%F A402839 a(p^k) = a(p^k-1) for primes p and integers k >= 1.
%F A402839 a(2*p) = a(2*p-1) for primes p >= 5.
%e A402839 a(6) = 4: 1 - 1/2 - 1/3 - 1/6 = 0, and no nonempty proper subsum is 0.
%K A402839 nonn,new
%O A402839 1,6
%A A402839 _Seiichi Manyama_, Nov 27 2026
